    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39244" root="نبض" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا بِهِ حَبَضٌ وَلَا نَبَضٌ</span></b> , (IDrd, S, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَبْضٌ</span>
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ولا نَبْضٌ</span></b> , (Sgh,) <i>There is not in him any motion:</i>
(S, Sgh, K:) or <i>sound,</i> or <i>voice, nor pulsation:</i>
(AA, in S, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حبض</span>:) or <i>strength:</i> (IDrd:)
with fet-h to the second letter, only used in a
negative phrase: (L:) As says, I know not what
is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَبَضُ</span>, (S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حبض</span>,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَبْضُ</span>. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُؤَادٌ نَبَضٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَبْضٌ</span>.

